{"cid": "UgzpZ5bh0cFpUWBWajZ4AaABAg", "text": "Hmm, are there other channels, where the stuff is explained for non-electronic engineers? I would need somebody to first tell me what all those capacitors are for. I know that voltage and energy flow are displaced by 90 degrees, and I know how to calculate the capacitance. But you start by saying \"very simple schematic\", but to me as a non-electrical engineer it looks like a bunch of random things connected. IT would really help if somebody would explain it like \"the stream of electrons starts to flow in here, then this or that happens at this capacitor, and then at this resistor the power is attentuated by this so that when those 2 streams meet it has this or that effect.\" But the way you explain it is like, I first have to understand it to understand it with your explanation.", "time": "2 months ago (edited)", "author": "@philipschroeder5427", "channel": "UCQvYBifUZcPXbvN6tluVtpQ", "votes": "0", "replies": "", "photo": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/ytc/AIdro_lR4rKyZmCdfGm4RxyEOPKYFL5xjS03I0SorfrRsfU=s88-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj", "heart": true, "reply": false, "time_parsed": 1761686847.582243}
